WEBVTT

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.580
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.580
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.580
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.920
One Hundred Billion Stars, One Hundred Billion Lights

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.920
Chapter 6

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:22.120
Kircheis. Where
are you, Kircheis ?

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:01.150
Kircheis !

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:10.260
I'd like you to disclose
your name and rank.

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:15.790
I want you to disclose
your name and rank !

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:30.680
Sinclair Cerebrese, Free Planets
Alliance Fleet, Vice Admiral.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:35.380
I ask for treatment
appropriate to my rank.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:40.830
Very well,
Vice Admiral Cerebrese.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:43.550
You are our prisoner of war.

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:48.010
If you pledge not to make any useless
resistance efforts, we will treat you honorably.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:52.060
Okay, I will make that pledge.

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:54.580
I will leave
myself in your care.

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.380
What is your name ?

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:02.660
Reinhard von Musel,
Galactic Imperial Navy, Commodore.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:04.900
Commodore ?

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:07.890
I see.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.310
This is a report to
Fleet Headquarters.

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:24.820
Commodore Reinhard von Musel has captured
a rebel commander named Sinclair Cerebrese.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:29.700
This man is ranked as a Vice
Admiral in the rebel forces...

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:34.440
...and has clearly expressed his intention to
leave himself in Commodore Musel's custody.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.100
I repeat.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:40.150
The rebel commander, Vice
Admiral Sinclair Cerebrese...

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:43.900
...has been captured by
Commodore Reinhard von Musel.

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:51.400
At this point, the Imperial Fleet had received
the withdraw order from Fleet Headquarters...

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:53.660
...and was preparing to pull back.

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:05.310
I see, you've done a fine job.

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:08.350
I will report that
to Fleet Headquarters.

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:11.280
It has already
been reported.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:18.370
His Excellency Grimmelshausen is aware of
Commodore Musel's delightful accomplishment.

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:24.490
I see, Lieutenant
Kircheis, you are quite...

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:29.650
...no, I commend you for your
loyalty to your superior.

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:35.190
But you shouldn't overdo it.

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:39.440
You should realize that you're
a soldier of the Imperial forces...

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:46.310
...not Commodore
Musel's private minion.

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:47.890
For your own sake, too.

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:55.640
Say, Kircheis...

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:57.560
Yes, Lord Reinhard.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:04.260
I've gotten you into lots of trouble, but
I want to burden you as little as possible...

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:06.410
...and I'd like
to share our glory.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:09.400
Those words are more
than enough for me.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:12.550
Besides, that Vice
Admiral Cerebrese...

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:16.320
...it's not like we can sever his body
in two and bring him in that way.

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:21.280
And it is an unmistakable
fact that you captured him.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.510
It is your accomplishment.

00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:25.920
Please don't pay attention
to what other people say.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:38.110
All this battle did was allow that
blond brat to make a name for himself.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:46.550
But in any case, that redhead, he's
much more than just a sub-officer.

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:51.190
Though no one seems to realize that since the blond brat's talents tend to draw everyone's attention.

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:56.440
On the other hand, what does the
blond brat himself think about him ?

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:04.150
If he doesn't know that, then
he's not a man of high caliber.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:07.900
Then he's like a peacock that
looks good but can't even fly.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:16.000
But since I lost glory to such a peacock, I guess
I don't have much to be commended for either.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:17.200
But that's alright.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:20.550
We've destroyed the enemy base
and accomplished our initial objective.

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:25.550
And we've been given a pullback
order, so it's better just to withdraw.

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:28.930
If I'm left behind on this barren
satellite, that would be miserable.

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:31.800
We'll withdraw as
soon as we're ready !

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:46.680
The Imperial forces
are pulling back !

00:07:56.960 --> 00:08:00.330
It looks like we're
saved, both of us.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:01.390
Yeah.

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:07.910
Because too many died already, I guess
Death's carriage got full before he got to us.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:16.830
This looks really bad.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.560
Linz, I'll leave you
in command here.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:24.050
I'll go take a look
at Headquarters.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:26.540
Blumhart, come with me.

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:48.430
It looks like they
invaded this area, too.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:00.570
Hey !

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:02.770
Yes, what can
I do for you ?

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:05.760
Who is that casualty ?

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:11.450
It's Lieutenant Junior Grade
Valery Lin Fitzsimmons.

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:15.820
She was shot to death
by an enemy soldier.

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:21.540
Would you like to see
her face, Lt. Colonel ?

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:30.090
No, that's fine.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:35.050
Oh, it's probably
needless to say this...

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:39.820
...but she'll get a special two-rank
promotion to Lieutenant Commander.

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:45.550
It's regrettable that it came after her death,
but it might be of some solace to the bereaved.

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:48.530
What do you mean
it's of "some solace" ?!

00:09:54.840 --> 00:10:03.050
Blumhart, there are too many
women I don't deserve to marry.

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:12.090
Despite it all,
when the spring comes...

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:19.810
...birds will return.

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:30.340
Despite it all,
when the spring comes...

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:37.230
...birds will return.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:41.950
What's that song ?

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:42.820
Huh ?

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:53.550
I think I memorized the
song without realizing it...

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:55.900
...because someone I used to
see sang it so many times.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:00.150
I don't remember anything
else about her, but...

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:01.620
It's strange, isn't it ?

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:11.400
But now you'll definitely be
the next regimental commander.

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:16.550
The 13th regimental commander
of the Knights of the Rose, eh ?

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:19.140
It's not such a bad
position, after all.

00:11:28.460 --> 00:11:32.370
The number of casualties
in Area #2 don't match up.

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:35.980
Don't concern yourself with
the exact numbers, young man.

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:41.060
In any case, so many people died,
about a million of them in all.

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:47.300
Even if it's a million and one to be exact, what
does it mean in the larger scheme of things ?

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:51.900
Then the casualties
are just numbers ?

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:57.010
Numbers where you don't mind at all
about rounding off their fractions ?

00:11:57.010 --> 00:11:59.350
That's exactly what it is
for the higher authorities.

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:01.850
Why are you so
impassioned about it ?

00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:07.130
The dead are just disposable items,
and we'll eventually be like that, too.

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:11.940
Then what are
we fighting for ?

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:17.200
Aren't we fighting to protect democracy
from those absolutist bastards ?

00:12:19.150 --> 00:12:21.270
Of course we are.

00:12:21.270 --> 00:12:25.190
We're knights upholding
justice against demons.

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:30.150
But the Imperial soldiers are
probably saying the same thing...

00:12:30.150 --> 00:12:35.300
...and even if they're demons, they
also have parents, siblings, or lovers.

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:38.170
We can't bother ourselves
to think about those things...

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:41.030
...so we'll just have to
count them all as numbers.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:46.170
You'll understand
that as well, some day.

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:01.910
Where's the Base Commander ?

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:08.720
He was lost during combat.

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:12.550
It seems he was
captured by the enemy.

00:13:21.220 --> 00:13:26.150
The base was destroyed and
the commander was captured.

00:13:26.150 --> 00:13:28.610
What a miserable outcome.

00:13:28.610 --> 00:13:31.250
I guess there are lots of
problems to take care of...

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:34.740
...before I'm officially appointed
as the regiment's commander.

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:46.020
The Battle of Van-Fleet Starzone dragged
on even after the ground battles ended...

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:51.630
...and it was already the end of April
when both fleets pulled back their forces.

00:14:01.010 --> 00:14:07.960
On May 15th, Reinhard and Kircheis
returned to the Imperial Capital, Odin.

00:14:15.510 --> 00:14:17.550
Although Reinhard was successful
during the ground battle...

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:23.150
...in that he made a name for himself
by capturing Vice Admiral Cerebrese...

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:29.980
...he did little in his area of
expertise, fleet warfare.

00:14:32.110 --> 00:14:39.020
For this reason, this was a battle that left him
with feelings of both delight and emptiness.

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:42.000
But because the space battle at Van-Fleet 4-2
as a whole became bogged down...

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:44.900
...the triumph in the ground combat
drew more attention as a result.

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:49.170
For that reason, Reinhard's
accomplishment was highly praised...

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:51.410
...and he was scheduled to be
promoted to Rear Admiral.

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:54.890
To be a Rear Admiral
at the age of 18...

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:58.930
...set the record for the youngest
Rear Admiral in the history of the Empire.

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:19.330
Hermann von Luneberg was also
promoted to Rear Admiral.

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:23.980
He was presumably promoted for the
feat of destroying the enemy base...

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:32.260
...but truthfully it may have been odd to promote his sub-captain, Reinhard, and not him.

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:48.020
Their direct superior, Grimmelshausen,
was also promoted, becoming a Admiral.

00:15:48.020 --> 00:15:51.690
For this advancement, it's said that some
the Ministry of the Military objected to it...

00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:55.170
...but it was realized with the
help of Emperor Friedrich IV.

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:57.650
There were also
other circumstances.

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:03.710
Promote that old man
to the rank of Admiral.

00:16:06.100 --> 00:16:11.640
He won't live much longer, so it's
okay to make him an Admiral.

00:16:14.050 --> 00:16:18.290
Besides, he'll probably never
go to the front line again.

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:25.980
With that statement, the Military and
the Emperor reached a compromise.

00:16:26.990 --> 00:16:31.530
In exchange for giving him the title of Admiral,
they can remove him from the front lines...

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:33.900
...and leave him to a
on the job vacation.

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:36.730
The three high admirals decided
to accept that compromise.

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:47.330
When all promotions and accolades
for the high officers were distributed...

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:49.930
...there was an incident
that enraged Reinhard.

00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:54.910
Kircheis was not promoted.

00:16:54.910 --> 00:17:00.030
Reinhard immediately went to complain to the manager of the personnel office, Vice Admiral Haupt.

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:09.370
If you say so, I can give Lt Kircheis
the rank of Lieutenant Commander.

00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:17.660
But in that case, I can't assign Lt. Commander
Kircheis to be your executive officer.

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:21.200
There has never been a precedent in
the history of the Imperial forces...

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:24.840
...of assigning a Lieutenant Commander
to serve directly under a Rear Admiral.

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:28.890
Though Haupt made this firm
assertion, it's not like he had proof.

00:17:28.890 --> 00:17:31.840
But no matter how talented Reinhard was,
there was no way he could've memorized...

00:17:31.840 --> 00:17:37.540
...all personnel assignments in the
500 year history of the Imperial forces.

00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:42.580
That shut the door on Reinhard's rebuttal, and he felt the personnel manager was being sly.

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:44.400
But the manager too had his own reasons.

00:17:45.570 --> 00:17:50.750
Since graduating from military school,
you've gotten unusually favored treatment...

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:56.130
...and the two of you have always received the same assignments.

00:17:56.130 --> 00:18:02.770
If you wish for Lieutenant Kircheis to be promoted, he'll have to be transferred.

00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:06.780
I'll do as you wish.

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:12.450
"Am I keeping Kircheis from promotion
because of my egocentrism ?"

00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:16.100
That was a bitter
realization for Reinhard.

00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:21.730
How did it go ?

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:23.650
Um, well...

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:35.030
Lord Reinhard, I don't want
to trouble you for my sake.

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:38.500
If the personnel manager dislikes
you, your position might be...

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:44.310
For Kircheis to be promoted,
shouldn't I liberate him from me ?

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:51.250
But what will happen to me
when I lose Kircheis's support ?

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:36.030
Welcome home.

00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:39.640
I'd like to congratulate
you on your safe return.

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:43.800
You've gotten even better at
saying things you don't mean.

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:48.540
Bring me some alcohol.

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:52.710
We have a white wine from Neue-Hessen
from the year 469, don't we ?

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:54.960
Could you bring it to us ?

00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:01.000
You bring it to me !

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:20.820
I've become a Rear Admiral.

00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:24.770
Congratulations.

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:27.760
What's there to
be happy about ?

00:20:28.610 --> 00:20:33.800
That Musel brat is a Rear Admiral,
the same rank as me, at the age of 18.

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:35.920
I'm already 35 years old.

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:41.300
By the time he becomes 35, he may
have already become a Fleet Admiral.

00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:49.940
Your fiancé was also a Rear
Admiral in his mid-twenties...

00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:52.550
...because he died in combat.

00:20:52.550 --> 00:20:55.260
You'll have to thank the
rebel army for that, I suppose.

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:59.550
Please don't talk about that.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:06.170
You're a cold woman
who won't open her heart.

00:21:07.480 --> 00:21:10.460
Is that how
I appear to you ?

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:13.840
If that's the case,
I'll try to change myself.

00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:16.220
I'll try so you won't
think of me that way.

00:21:18.310 --> 00:21:19.930
I wonder what will
come out of it.

00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:23.730
I don't think you'll
ever open your heart to me.

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:29.150
You'll always think
about your dead fiancé.

00:21:29.690 --> 00:21:34.050
It's kind of amusing for me to see
that you believe that he's still alive...

00:21:34.050 --> 00:21:37.630
...and hope that he'll
come back someday.

00:21:52.550 --> 00:21:56.330
I will go visit High Admiral
Ovlessor tomorrow.

00:21:56.330 --> 00:22:00.490
I can't go without greeting him now
that I've been promoted to Rear Admiral.

00:22:01.150 --> 00:22:05.710
After all, he's the chief commander
of the Empire in ground warfare.

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:10.410
That's good for you.

00:22:10.870 --> 00:22:13.830
You're talking like it's
someone else's business.

00:22:14.450 --> 00:22:16.550
You're supposed
to come with me.

00:22:18.360 --> 00:22:19.570
What's the matter ?

00:22:19.570 --> 00:22:25.070
No matter how brutal High Admiral
Ovlessor is, it's not like he'll eat you alive.

00:22:25.070 --> 00:22:33.650
I heard he doesn't have an appetite
unless it's meat in hard armor...

00:22:39.550 --> 00:22:43.900
In any case, Madame, since
we're husband and wife...

00:22:43.900 --> 00:22:47.410
...we should do the usual
business of a husband and wife...

00:22:58.630 --> 00:23:04.300
Well, well, I'm glad to see you both
safely home, Mr Blond and Mr Red-head.

00:23:04.300 --> 00:23:09.650
I was worried you might be
bullied by malicious superiors.

00:23:11.660 --> 00:23:19.550
If you're smart, strong-willed and handsome,
people tend to pick on you, even in school.

00:23:19.550 --> 00:23:25.150
Especially since Mr Blond is the
type that the superiors tend to detest.

00:23:31.750 --> 00:23:33.320
How about dinner ?

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:36.050
Please don't worry -
we had it already.

00:23:36.820 --> 00:23:39.230
It's late already,
so we'll go to bed soon.

00:23:40.050 --> 00:23:44.090
Besides, we have to go to the Ministry
of Military Affairs in the morning, so...

00:23:44.090 --> 00:23:45.630
Oh...

00:23:46.680 --> 00:23:52.850
But I didn't know that military
officers were such busy people.

00:23:52.850 --> 00:23:59.260
My late husband was always
fishing when he wasn't off to war.

00:23:59.260 --> 00:24:03.150
But of course, he never got
further than Lieutenant.

00:24:03.150 --> 00:24:05.310
My husband was
like that, too.

00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:08.780
Well, we'll go...

00:24:10.230 --> 00:24:16.690
Then I'll bring you some wine,
to celebrate your safe return home.

00:24:17.550 --> 00:24:19.330
Are you sure it's okay ?

00:24:19.330 --> 00:24:21.960
You two are
already grown up.

00:24:27.710 --> 00:24:34.910
That night, Reinhard received a notice that
he'd been granted a meeting with Annerose.

00:24:36.150 --> 00:24:38.900
That news undoubtedly delighted him...

00:24:38.900 --> 00:24:41.860
...much more than battlefield
accomplishments or promotions.

00:24:40.470 --> 00:24:46.100
Chronicle of the Aftermath of the Chaotic War

00:24:48.020 --> 00:24:57.220
 Even as I say it's beautiful. Even as I say it's magnificent

00:24:48.150 --> 00:24:52.380
[ Aurora's Adagio ]

00:24:48.150 --> 00:24:52.380
Ending Theme

00:24:48.150 --> 00:24:52.380
Vocals: Ogura Kei

00:24:53.080 --> 00:24:57.340
Reinhard:

00:24:53.080 --> 00:24:57.340
Horikawa Ryo

00:24:58.460 --> 00:25:08.020
 Words fall short and I can only be amazed

00:24:58.660 --> 00:25:02.890
Luneberg:

00:24:58.660 --> 00:25:02.890
Nozawa Nachi

00:25:03.860 --> 00:25:07.950
Schenkopp:

00:25:03.860 --> 00:25:07.950
Hazama Michio

00:25:09.010 --> 00:25:14.520
 Darkness is a dance that flees and continues

00:25:14.160 --> 00:25:18.100
Friedrich:

00:25:14.160 --> 00:25:18.100
Saka Osamu

00:25:14.520 --> 00:25:17.870
 Time is a drama that vanishes and writes itself

00:25:19.260 --> 00:25:28.870
 All of those are mysteries. The miracle of the aurora is glistening

